# CaramOS (caramos-ota): defaults that must win over Linux Mint's mint-artwork.gschema.override.
# glib-compile-schemas reads the override files in name order and the last value of a key wins. "mint-artwork" sorts
# after the ISO's 99_caramos override, so Mint's "Ubuntu" fonts won on the Cinnamon lock screen and on the login
# screen (slick-greeter), which on the Xfce edition is also the lock screen. These keys are set again here, in a file
# that sorts after Mint's. Anyone who chose a font of their own keeps it: these are only defaults.
[org.cinnamon.desktop.screensaver]
font-date='Be Vietnam Pro 24'
font-message='Be Vietnam Pro 14'
font-time='Be Vietnam Pro 64'

[x.dm.slick-greeter]
font-name='Be Vietnam Pro 11'
